TYPES.md §8.1: the codes of a @codes enum are unique, retired members included; an enum without
@codes has no codes to compare.
-- teamboard/vocab.canon --
package teamboard

enum Element @codes(UInt8) { FIRE = 1, retired WIND = 4, WATER = 2, STORM = 4, BLAZE = 1 }

enum Tone { warm, cold }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3102]  teamboard/vocab.canon:3:77
  code 4 is used twice (first at teamboard/vocab.canon:3)
  expected by teamboard/vocab.canon:3 (@codes(UInt8))

error[E3102]  teamboard/vocab.canon:3:88
  code 1 is used twice (first at teamboard/vocab.canon:3)
  expected by teamboard/vocab.canon:3 (@codes(UInt8))

